  "preamble": "The voiced alveolo-palatal fricative [ʑ] becomes the plain voiceless alveolar fricative [s] through devoicing and depalatalization together. The Middle Chinese 船 initial, reconstructed as /ʑ/ by Zhengzhang Shangfang, Pan Wuyun and Pulleyblank (Li Rong and Wang Li reconstruct /dʑ/ instead), gives s in Standard Cantonese, where the voiced obstruents devoiced and the palatal and dental sibilants merged. Sino-Korean and Kan-on Sino-Japanese s are left out: both were borrowed from Late Middle Chinese, by which time this initial had already merged into a retroflex series.",
